# Hostfile for bin/tp_ddp_cluster.dart — 3D (data × tensor) parallelism.
#
# One line per HOST = one data-parallel rank. The second column is that
# rank's tensor-parallel GPU set (comma-separated ordinals), passed as
# TP_DEVICES. Omit it to use every visible GPU on the host.
#
# Format:  host[:user@]   gpu-set
#
# The first non-comment line is rank 0 and the rendezvous master
# (override with --master-addr). Lines starting with # are ignored.

# Two hosts, each tensor-parallel across its 4 GPUs (world size 2):
10.0.0.1   0,1,2,3
10.0.0.2   0,1,2,3

# Mixed example: host with a user, and a host using only 2 of its GPUs:
# user@10.0.0.3   0,1
# 10.0.0.4                 # (no gpu-set -> all visible GPUs)
